# Caddy, the only service that publishes ports (AD-2, AD-26). Two sites:
#   *.<zone>        the Tenant zone wildcard, proxied to Host.Hosted
#   <admin host>    the Admin hostname, proxied to Host.Admin
# It shares a network with those two hosts only, and none with the worker, PostgreSQL or
# OpenBao. Hosts listen for health on loopback only, so no health port is reachable either.
#
# Everything else gets no content: an unknown name fails the TLS handshake, because Caddy
# holds no certificate for it; a Host header that isn't the name the TLS handshake was for
# gets an empty 421, so one site's connection never reaches the other; plain HTTP redirects
# only the two sites, with no body, and closes every other request with no response.
#
# Settings, from the caddy service's environment (deploy/compose.yaml), checked by start.sh
# before Caddy starts:
#   GATEKEEP_TENANT_ZONE  the Tenant zone; *.<zone> is served, the zone apex is not.
#   GATEKEEP_ADMIN_HOST   the Admin hostname, never under the zone.
#   GATEKEEP_TLS_MODE     internal (Caddy's local CA, for local and CI) or cloudflare, set
#                         only by deploy/compose.cloudflare.yaml
#                         (production: publicly trusted certificates by ACME DNS-01 through
#                         Cloudflare DNS, tls-cloudflare.caddy).
#
# Caddy listens on 8080 and 8443 inside the container, so it needs no capability to bind;
# Compose publishes them as the host's 80 and 443.

{
	# No admin API, and no config written back to disk.
	admin off
	persist_config off

	http_port 8080
	https_port 8443

	# Redirects are written below, so that they carry no port and cover the two sites only.
	auto_https disable_redirects
	# The internal CA's root stays in Caddy's data volume: never installed anywhere.
	skip_install_trust

	servers {
		# Only TCP 443 is published, so no HTTP/3 advertisement.
		protocols h1 h2
		# The Host header must be the name the TLS handshake was for: 421 otherwise.
		strict_sni_host on
	}
}

# Defines the tenant-tls and admin-tls snippets for the chosen mode.
import tls-{$GATEKEEP_TLS_MODE}.caddy

# Each host reaches Caddy over its own edge network, so a request from the other host's
# edge subnet (fixed in deploy/compose.yaml) is code in that host using Caddy as a bridge:
# the connection closes with no response. Host.Hosted can't reach Host.Admin through Caddy,
# nor Host.Admin a Tenant site.
https://*.{$GATEKEEP_TENANT_ZONE} {
	import tenant-tls
	@from_admin_edge remote_ip 10.201.2.0/24
	abort @from_admin_edge
	header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
	reverse_proxy hosted:8080
}

https://{$GATEKEEP_ADMIN_HOST} {
	import admin-tls
	@from_hosted_edge remote_ip 10.201.1.0/24
	abort @from_hosted_edge
	header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
	reverse_proxy admin:8080
}

http://*.{$GATEKEEP_TENANT_ZONE}, http://{$GATEKEEP_ADMIN_HOST} {
	redir https://{host}{uri} 308
}

# Any other name over plain HTTP: the connection closes with no response.
http:// {
	abort
}
